The SVGs are the originals and are kept for provenance; the shell loads the
PNGs beside them. Qt's own SVG renderer draws these files wrong -- cropped, on
an opaque field -- so they are rasterised at install time instead:

    for f in *.svg; do magick -background none "$f" -resize 512x512 "${f%.svg}.png"; done
